.title = "ANSI Terminal",
.date = "2026-09-30",
.author = "ZigCC",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

ANSI escape codes can style terminal output without an additional package. This example
collects commonly used styles, foreground colors, screen operations, and cursor controls in
one `Ansi` helper. `Ansi.print` applies a style and always resets it, while constants can be
combined at compile time, such as `Ansi.bold ++ Ansi.green`.

The same pattern can be extended with background colors, 256-color sequences, or application-
specific styles. Always reset styling after output so later terminal text is not affected.

